            "kind": "REWORK",
            "comments": [
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 38,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Harshit Aghera",
                        "email": "haghera@nvidia.com",
                        "username": "harshit-aghera"
                    },
                    "message": "Add info about platform used for testing."
                },
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 38,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Eric Liu",
                        "email": "liuer@nvidia.com",
                        "username": "liuer-sys"
                    },
                    "message": "Done.See PS7: https://gerrit.openbmc.org/c/openbmc/bmcweb/+/88035/7/COMMIT_MSG"
                },
                {
                    "file": "redfish-core/lib/processor.hpp",
                    "line": 827,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Harshit Aghera",
                        "email": "haghera@nvidia.com",
                        "username": "harshit-aghera"
                    },
                    "message": "For errors other than boost::system::errc::io_error or EBADR, we should log error report messages::internalError."
                },
                {
                    "file": "redfish-core/lib/processor.hpp",
                    "line": 827,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Eric Liu",
                        "email": "liuer@nvidia.com",
                        "username": "liuer-sys"
                    },
                    "message": "Done. EBADR and io_error return silently, other errors log BMCWEB_LOG_ERROR and return messages::internalError. Same pattern as fabric.hpp.\nSee PS7: https://gerrit.openbmc.org/c/openbmc/bmcweb/+/88035/7/redfish-core/lib/processor.hpp#827"
                },
                {
                    "file": "redfish-core/lib/processor.hpp",
                    "line": 832,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Harshit Aghera",
                        "email": "haghera@nvidia.com",
                        "username": "harshit-aghera"
                    },
                    "message": "Should we log error for multiple memory objects or do the summation for Total Memory size across all the memory objects? @ed@tanous.net, @gunnar@gmills.xyz, your input here will help."
                },
                {
                    "file": "redfish-core/lib/processor.hpp",
                    "line": 832,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Eric Liu",
                        "email": "liuer@nvidia.com",
                        "username": "liuer-sys"
                    },
                    "message": "Thanks, Harshit, for raising this question.\n\nAfter survey this, the DMTF Processor v1_18_0 schema longDescription for MemorySummary.TotalMemorySizeMiB (schema link):\nhttps://redfish.dmtf.org/schemas/v1/Processor.v1_18_0.json\n\n\"This property shall contain the total size of non-cache, volatile or non-volatile memory attached to this processor. Examples include DRAMs and NV-DIMMs that are not configured as block storage. This value indicates the size of memory directly attached or with strong affinity to this processor, not the total memory accessible by the processor. This property shall not be present for implementations where all processors have equal memory performance or access characteristics, such as hop count, for all system memory.\"\n\nThe schema defines this property directly as \"total size ... attached to this processor\" \u2014 the aggregated capacity across all memory objects attached to that processor.\n\nPS8 has been updated to implement this schema semantic: summing MemorySizeInKB across all endpoints returned by the containing association.\n\nIf I've misinterpreted this, I'm happy to update. Thanks very much."
                },
                {
                    "file": "redfish-core/lib/processor.hpp",
                    "line": 842,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Harshit Aghera",
                        "email": "haghera@nvidia.com",
                        "username": "harshit-aghera"
                    },
                    "message": "Add comment about unit conversion from D-Bus to redfish."
                },
                {
                    "file": "redfish-core/lib/processor.hpp",
                    "line": 842,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Eric Liu",
                        "email": "liuer@nvidia.com",
                        "username": "liuer-sys"
                    },
                    "message": "Done. Added \"// Convert D-Bus MemorySizeInKB (KiB) to Redfish TotalMemorySizeMiB (MiB)\".\nSee PS7: https://gerrit.openbmc.org/c/openbmc/bmcweb/+/88035/7/redfish-core/lib/processor.hpp#854"
                },
                {
                    "file": "redfish-core/lib/processor.hpp",
                    "line": 852,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Harshit Aghera",
                        "email": "haghera@nvidia.com",
                        "username": "harshit-aghera"
                    },
                    "message": "use sdbusplus::object_path operator /."
                },
                {
                    "file": "redfish-core/lib/processor.hpp",
                    "line": 852,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Eric Liu",
                        "email": "liuer@nvidia.com",
                        "username": "liuer-sys"
                    },
                    "message": "Done. Changed to sdbusplus::message::object_path(objectPath) / \"containing\".\nSee PS7: https://gerrit.openbmc.org/c/openbmc/bmcweb/+/88035/7/redfish-core/lib/processor.hpp#869"
                }
            ],
