            },
            "createdOn": 1776849362,
            "author": {
                "name": "Eric Liu",
                "email": "liuer@nvidia.com",
                "username": "liuer-sys"
            },
            "kind": "REWORK",
            "comments": [
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 48,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Eric Liu",
                        "email": "liuer@nvidia.com",
                        "username": "liuer-sys"
                    },
                    "message": "Done."
                },
                {
                    "file": "redfish-core/lib/processor.hpp",
                    "line": 837,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Eric Liu",
                        "email": "liuer@nvidia.com",
                        "username": "liuer-sys"
                    },
                    "message": "Done. Aggregation behavior changed as follows:\n\nBefore:\n  TotalMemorySizeMiB is written only when ALL endpoints succeed\n  (endpointsFound && allSuccess). A single EBADR/io_error hides the\n  whole property.\n\nAfter:\n  TotalMemorySizeMiB is written when AT LEAST ONE endpoint is\n  successfully aggregated. Endpoints returning EBADR or io_error are\n  logged at debug level and skipped; any other D-Bus error sets\n  hasError and results in messages::internalError.\n\nImplementation:\n  1. Removed allSuccess entirely.\n  2. Moved acc->endpointsFound = true from the association callback\n     into the success path of afterGetMemorySize.\n  3. Destructor condition reduced to `if (endpointsFound)`.\n\nSee PS10:\n  - gate:            https://gerrit.openbmc.org/c/openbmc/bmcweb/+/88035/10/redfish-core/lib/processor.hpp#836\n  - endpointsFound:  https://gerrit.openbmc.org/c/openbmc/bmcweb/+/88035/10/redfish-core/lib/processor.hpp#875"
                },
                {
                    "file": "redfish-core/lib/processor.hpp",
                    "line": 975,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Eric Liu",
                        "email": "liuer@nvidia.com",
                        "username": "liuer-sys"
                    },
                    "message": "Done. Switched to getAssociatedSubTree and removed afterGetMemoryService; the service map from the mapper is now used directly, avoiding the per-endpoint getDbusObject calls.\n\nSee PS10: https://gerrit.openbmc.org/c/openbmc/bmcweb/+/88035/10/redfish-core/lib/processor.hpp#942"
                }
            ],
